<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__0118__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 893" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n893/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cochineal used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 893"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Lac yields a fine red dye, which, though not so bright as the true Mexican cochineal, is said to be more permanent; and the resinous part is extensively used in the manufacture of sealing-wax and hats, and as a varnish."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
